- **`tests/test_ensure_capture.py`** (new) — 9 tests covering all Checkpoint A cases.

## Key implementation decisions
- **Filename canonical token** achieved by passing `pack_version=f"{source_kind}-{sha7}"` to `build_cache` (it derives `{pack}@{version}.json` from that field); registry version lives in provenance as `registry_pack_version`. `evidence_identity = f"on_demand:{rung}:{full_sha}"`, `git_commit = clone rev-parse`.
- **Tier guard**: stub-indexed/stub-stamped/unattested/no-pin → tier −1 (replaceable); attested non-on-demand kinds rank runtime (real captures beat static parses); same-or-higher → per-class no-op.
- **Hygiene strip refinement found while writing tests**: blind "strip everything not newly captured" would orphan classes already homed in the *same* versioned file when a second extract of the same pack at the same tier+commit adds a class. Strip now keeps `captured ∪ {classes whose prior index row points at this file}`. Mixed-pack R (index→runtime file) is still stripped exactly.

